Template: tachyon-validator/user
Type: string
Default: x1
Description: User/Group to run tachyon-validator as:
 Specify the system user that will run the tachyon-validator service.
 The user will be created if it doesn't exist.

Template: tachyon-validator/home
Type: string
Default:
Description: Home directory for validator data:
 Specify the home directory for the validator. This is where the
 validator.sh script and data will be stored. Leave empty to use
 /var/lib/<user>.

Template: tachyon-validator/validator_script_path
Type: string
Default:
Description: Path to validator.sh script:
 Specify the path where the validator.sh script is stored.
 Leave empty to use <home>/validator.sh.

Template: tachyon-validator/log_path
Type: string
Default: /var/log/tachyon-validator.log
Description: Log file path:
 Specify the path for validator logs. Leave empty to use journald
 (view with: journalctl -u tachyon-validator).

Template: tachyon-validator/network
Type: select
Choices: mainnet, testnet
Default: mainnet
Description: Network:
 Select which network this validator will connect to.

Template: tachyon-validator/mode
Type: select
Choices: validator, validator-rpc, rpc-readonly
Default: validator
Description: Validator mode:
 Select the operating mode for this validator:
 .
 validator: Voting validator without RPC (lowest resource usage)
 .
 validator-rpc: Voting validator with RPC enabled
 .
 rpc-readonly: Non-voting RPC node (no vote account required)
